WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.467
-Welcome, welcome,
welcome, welcome to

00:00:02.467 --> 00:00:04.267
"The Tonight Show," everybody.
You're here.

00:00:04.267 --> 00:00:07.734
[ Cheers and applause ]
That's a hot crowd.

00:00:07.734 --> 00:00:11.467
Guys, I hope everyone's
having a good fall/summer/sauna.

00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:13.067
[ Laughter ]

00:00:13.067 --> 00:00:14.234
Yep, here in New York City,

00:00:14.234 --> 00:00:17.400
the temperature was up
in the high 70s.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.234
Yeah, apparently, we turned
the clocks back an hour

00:00:19.234 --> 00:00:20.567
and the calendar by four months.

00:00:20.567 --> 00:00:22.200
[ Laughter ]

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:24.300
Usually when you hear "November"
and "mid 70s,"

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:26.200
it's about every candidate
running for president.

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:30.968
[ Laughter ]

00:00:30.968 --> 00:00:32.300
Well, speaking of New York City,

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:34.100
this weekend was
the New York City Marathon.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:37.567
And congrats to any of the
runners out there watching.

00:00:37.567 --> 00:00:39.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:39.501 --> 00:00:41.467
Anyone in the audience
run the marathon?

00:00:41.467 --> 00:00:43.300
[ Cheers and applause ]
Hey!

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:44.501
Congratulations.

00:00:44.501 --> 00:00:45.701
You had a lot of support
out there --

00:00:45.701 --> 00:00:48.767
people handing out water,
Gatorade, bananas, I saw.

00:00:48.767 --> 00:00:50.934
I saw a lot of people
with signs,

00:00:50.934 --> 00:00:52.534
some signs
I've never seen before.

00:00:52.534 --> 00:00:54.000
It's kind of odd.
I took some pictures.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:55.534
Take a look at this.
This one said...

00:00:57.901 --> 00:00:59.701
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.701 --> 00:01:01.033
-Wow.

00:01:01.033 --> 00:01:02.534
-Then there was this one.
It says...

00:01:05.267 --> 00:01:06.934
[ Laughter ]
Why would you --

00:01:06.934 --> 00:01:08.267
And finally,
I saw this one that said...

00:01:10.734 --> 00:01:11.767
[ Laughter ]
You know that's not --

00:01:11.767 --> 00:01:12.868
Doesn't help anyone.

00:01:12.868 --> 00:01:14.734
-I think he knows.
-Let's get to some news.

00:01:14.734 --> 00:01:18.000
Big week in politics,
'cause tomorrow is Election Day.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:20.601
Yep, as we speak, Instagram is
being flooded with two things --

00:01:20.601 --> 00:01:22.534
marathon medals
and "I voted" stickers.

00:01:22.534 --> 00:01:23.667
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.667 --> 00:01:24.968
That's right,
the midterms are tomorrow,

00:01:24.968 --> 00:01:26.434
which means
you're gonna see a lot of people

00:01:26.434 --> 00:01:28.300
walking around with their
"I voted" stickers.

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:29.567
And this year, there's actually

00:01:29.567 --> 00:01:31.434
a bunch of voting stickers
to choose from.

00:01:31.434 --> 00:01:32.601
For instance, there's the...

00:01:35.367 --> 00:01:36.601
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.601 --> 00:01:37.701
Next, there's...

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:41.968
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:43.133
Next up...

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:48.067
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.067 --> 00:01:49.234
Next, there's...

00:01:52.567 --> 00:01:54.000
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:55.167
And finally...

00:01:58.701 --> 00:02:01.801
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:02:01.801 --> 00:02:07.434
Yeah, but it --
[ Both laugh ]

00:02:07.434 --> 00:02:09.734
Speaking of midterms,
on Saturday, President Biden,

00:02:09.734 --> 00:02:12.334
former president Obama,
and former president Trump

00:02:12.334 --> 00:02:15.667
were all campaigning in
Pennsylvania at the same time.

00:02:15.667 --> 00:02:17.968
'Cause there's no better way
to win over voters

00:02:17.968 --> 00:02:20.367
than by shutting down every
highway in the entire state.

00:02:20.367 --> 00:02:22.100
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:23.467
And during his rally
in Pennsylvania,

00:02:23.467 --> 00:02:24.934
people were talking about
how Trump came up

00:02:24.934 --> 00:02:27.801
with a new nickname for
Florida governor Ron DeSantis.

00:02:27.801 --> 00:02:28.934
Listen to this.

00:02:28.934 --> 00:02:30.601
-We're winning big, big, big

00:02:30.601 --> 00:02:33.467
in the Republican Party
for the nomination.

00:02:33.467 --> 00:02:35.200
Trump at 71%.

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:38.734
Ron DeSanctimonious at 10%.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.734 --> 00:02:41.367
-Yeah.
"Ron DeSanctimonious."

00:02:41.367 --> 00:02:42.501
[ Laughter ]

00:02:42.501 --> 00:02:43.801
Trump doesn't even know
what that means.

00:02:43.801 --> 00:02:45.501
He thought he was casting
a Harry Potter spell on him.

00:02:45.501 --> 00:02:48.367
He was like,
"Ron Expecto DeSanctimonius."

00:02:48.367 --> 00:02:51.100
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:54.167
"Expecto Sanctimonius!
Ron.

00:02:54.167 --> 00:02:55.634
I should've just went
with Ron Weasley.

00:02:55.634 --> 00:02:56.834
That was right there.
Why didn't I do --"

00:02:56.834 --> 00:02:58.067
[ Laughter ]

00:02:58.067 --> 00:02:59.467
Well, with
the midterm elections tomorrow,

00:02:59.467 --> 00:03:01.601
there's not much time left
to learn about the candidates,

00:03:01.601 --> 00:03:03.167
so we thought we'd help you out
by showing you

00:03:03.167 --> 00:03:05.367
all of their
campaign ads at once.

00:03:05.367 --> 00:03:07.467
It's time for a "Campaign Cram."
Here we go.

00:03:07.467 --> 00:03:10.567
♪♪

00:03:10.567 --> 00:03:11.601
-Hi.
-Hello.

00:03:11.601 --> 00:03:13.367
-Hey.
-I'm running for...Congress.

00:03:13.367 --> 00:03:15.734
Because...in this country,
we...make breakfast.

00:03:15.734 --> 00:03:18.667
-And...I shot my...mom...
for no good reason at all.

00:03:18.667 --> 00:03:21.834
It was sneaky...
but...I don't care.

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:24.567
She was a...racist,
and...I am...damn proud of it.

00:03:24.567 --> 00:03:27.567
So...for some reason,
I approve this message.

00:03:27.567 --> 00:03:28.667
♪♪

00:03:28.667 --> 00:03:30.667
-There you go.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:30.667 --> 00:03:32.167
There you go.
Make the right choice.

00:03:32.167 --> 00:03:36.100
[ Applause ]

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:38.234
Meanwhile, tomorrow,
several states will vote

00:03:38.234 --> 00:03:40.501
on recreational marijuana
legalization.

00:03:40.501 --> 00:03:42.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:42.934 --> 00:03:44.534
And politicians
on both sides of the aisle

00:03:44.534 --> 00:03:45.934
are speaking out about it.

00:03:45.934 --> 00:03:47.667
Here, check out what some of
them are trying to say here.

00:03:47.667 --> 00:03:49.834
First up, Congressman
Michael Cloud said...

00:03:54.501 --> 00:03:56.901
[ Laughter ]

00:03:56.901 --> 00:03:58.968
And Congressman Ted Budd said...

00:04:03.133 --> 00:04:04.968
[ Laughter ]

00:04:04.968 --> 00:04:06.968
Up next,
Senator Tom Cotton said...

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:11.400
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:13.400
And Congressman
Jared Huffman said...

00:04:17.634 --> 00:04:19.601
[ Laughter ]

00:04:19.601 --> 00:04:24.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:24.601 --> 00:04:26.601
Congressman Colin Allred said...

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:30.968
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.968 --> 00:04:33.000
Congresswoman Anna Eshoo said...

00:04:38.501 --> 00:04:41.200
[ Laughter ]

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:43.200
Congressman Don Bacon said...

00:04:48.067 --> 00:04:49.167
[ Laughter ]

00:04:49.167 --> 00:04:51.000
[ Rimshot ]

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:53.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:53.734 --> 00:04:56.767
-Don...

00:04:56.767 --> 00:04:59.667
-He didn't understand.

00:04:59.667 --> 00:05:01.734
Then Congressman
Dan Newhouse said...

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:06.400
[ Laughter ]

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:08.534
Congressman Barry Moore said...

00:05:12.334 --> 00:05:15.200
[ Laughter ]

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:17.267
And, finally,
Senator Roy Blunt said...

00:05:19.367 --> 00:05:20.868
Yeah, there you go.

00:05:20.868 --> 00:05:25.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:25.868 --> 00:05:27.567
You guys see everyone's talking
about Elon Musk

00:05:27.567 --> 00:05:29.701
taking over Twitter,
and now a bunch of people

00:05:29.701 --> 00:05:31.968
have been tweeting
under the name Elon Musk.

00:05:31.968 --> 00:05:33.334
[ Laughter ]

00:05:33.334 --> 00:05:35.334
So they're saying stuff
that he wouldn't normally say.

00:05:35.334 --> 00:05:38.501
Now Elon is threatening
to ban impersonation accounts

00:05:38.501 --> 00:05:41.334
that don't label themselves
as parody.

00:05:41.334 --> 00:05:43.234
Of course, nobody knows
whether Elon Musk said that

00:05:43.234 --> 00:05:44.901
or if it was
from a parody account.

00:05:44.901 --> 00:05:47.467
[ Laughter ]
Sounds right.

00:05:47.467 --> 00:05:48.801
Hey, I want to say
congratulations to

00:05:48.801 --> 00:05:52.234
the Houston Astros on winning
the 2022 World Series.

00:05:52.234 --> 00:05:58.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:58.801 --> 00:06:01.167
It's a big -- It's big
for Astros star pitcher

00:06:01.167 --> 00:06:03.434
Justin Verlander.
He's almost 40,

00:06:03.434 --> 00:06:04.968
just won
his second championship,

00:06:04.968 --> 00:06:06.534
and he's married
to a supermodel.

00:06:06.534 --> 00:06:07.534
Tom Brady was like,

00:06:07.534 --> 00:06:08.868
[voice breaking]
"Congratulations."

00:06:08.868 --> 00:06:14.734
[ Laughter ]

00:06:14.734 --> 00:06:17.033
I heard that more than
50 students in Texas

00:06:17.033 --> 00:06:19.901
may have to retake their SATs
after the test sheets

00:06:19.901 --> 00:06:21.334
flew out of a UPS truck.

00:06:21.334 --> 00:06:23.000
[ Audience groans ]

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:24.767
Students should've known
this was going to happen

00:06:24.767 --> 00:06:26.501
because one of the questions
on the test was,

00:06:26.501 --> 00:06:29.200
"If a UPS truck is driving
at 50 miles per hour

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:33.501
with the trunk open..."
[ Laughter ]

00:06:33.501 --> 00:06:36.267
"And another UPS --"

00:06:36.267 --> 00:06:38.601
Get this -- a JCPenney in
Pennsylvania had to be

00:06:38.601 --> 00:06:42.000
closed temporarily
after a deer entered the store

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:45.100
and got into a dressing room.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:45.100 --> 00:06:47.167
That story, again --
JCPenney is so empty,

00:06:47.167 --> 00:06:48.934
it's actually
being reclaimed by nature.

00:06:48.934 --> 00:06:52.901
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:52.901 --> 00:06:54.701
"Get out.
Get out.

00:06:54.701 --> 00:06:57.334
My place.
Get out."

00:06:57.334 --> 00:06:58.934
[ Chuckles ]

00:06:58.934 --> 00:07:00.701
Well, listen to this --
a New York fugitive

00:07:00.701 --> 00:07:02.234
who had been on the run
for almost a year

00:07:02.234 --> 00:07:03.968
was just caught at Disney World.

00:07:03.968 --> 00:07:05.434
[ Laughter ]
Yep, they caught him

00:07:05.434 --> 00:07:08.033
right before he crossed the
international border into Epcot.

00:07:08.033 --> 00:07:10.801
[ Laughter ]

